	(text "R1 converts SiPM \ncurrent pulse \nto voltage\n\n--Why 49.9--\ntradeoff: bigger R => \nbigger V \nbut slower recovery \ntime from \nSiPM's capacitors. \nMuon is\nrare enough that\nwe don't need\nfast recovery time."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 33.02 91.186 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0afc16b0-100d-4314-a19e-cdfad235aa97")
	)
	(text "BASELINE FILTER\nde-noises the 50 mV divider.\nCaps direct noise to ground.\nC9 covers 70 Hz to few MHz.\nC10 covers after few MHz."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 44.958 117.094 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0d6620b8-59a9-44d8-affb-caaee22f2267")
	)
	(text "SIGNAL INJECTION - test the amplifier without a SiPM"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 242.57 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "126ea867-3b75-4594-a318-9c64d4a6bc26")
	)
	(text "J1 is the cable \nconnector to Grant's \npower/interface board.\n------------\nPin 1,3,5 brings\npower in. Pin 7 \nsends TRIG \nout to the FPGA\n------------\nEvery signal is paired \nwith an adjacent GRND so \nits return current \nhas a short path right \nbeside it. That keeps \nthe loop area small, \nwhich limits both what \nthe cable radiates \nand what it picks up.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 205.486 168.402 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "13b49b95-37d2-4c2a-a62b-e8e8b5a1b6ab")
	)
	(text "cable has its\nown impedance.\nR7 smooths out\noverall V output\n---------\nThe target is R7 + \ndriver output \nimpedance ≈ cable \nimpedance"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 379.984 138.938 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2c00c6cd-74ce-4c62-9f37-801f5699258e")
	)
	(text "Voltage-divider circuit:\nV_out \n= V_in × R4/(R3+R4)\n= 0.050 V.\nso, V_out going into \nU1B's + pin is 50 mV "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.078 108.204 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "433f6707-04d0-464c-938e-64b831eba725")
	)
	(text "SiPM BIAS FILTER\nC8-R9 form low-pass filter to let steady 27V through.\nC7 supplies fast current source to SiPM.\nPlace C7 and C8 right beside the SiPM on the PCB."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 54.356 23.114 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "495b20e2-284e-49b8-a7c7-245c93166eff")
	)
	(text "OPTIONAL PARTS - DNP (not fitted unless bench tests need them)\nR19 adds ~10 mV of hysteresis. D3 clamps COMP_IN between GND and 3.3 V.\nC11 sits across R5 (12.4k): U1A stability option."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 355.092 69.088 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "58a1ed6c-a8fd-43a4-b0cc-d77ef17d6804")
	)
	(text "U2: VOLTAGE-COMPARATOR"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 252.476 66.802 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "693c3eb1-a4fd-4ea5-aa9e-9264b6fc1ba2")
	)
	(text "R5 combined with \nstray C at the − input \ncan cause ringing \nif it's too large."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 191.77 59.436 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6d4021a4-d41e-46dd-9680-6f63121a5c27")
	)
	(text "Why R2=499 ohms:\n1) low thermal noise V = √(4kTRB)\ngoing into U1A's + pin.\n2) balanced high-pass filter.\n3) op-amp pushes small current\nout the + pin, high R means high\nunwanted V.\nNot magic #(300 or 1k would also work)\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 126.238 84.836 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6d9f9bcf-aea6-4440-8837-264ec6df5af2")
	)
	(text "U1C sets max\n& min of U1A output\n---------------\n5V leaves room for\nmassive high V\nevents from SiPM."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 255.778 111.252 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "83ea87eb-6885-4f8d-a81b-cf41f019d4d2")
	)
	(text "U1B's job is to produce a constant tiny voltage\nVBASE (50 mV) that U1A uses as baseline.\n\nU1A can't use 0 as baseline because the AC\ncoupling from C1 forces a 0 average V so \n(+) pulses will force (-) pulses after, \nand when (-) V are fed into op-amps, they \nneed time to recover & ruin signal integrity.\n\nWe're using a V divider to get \nthat tiny V, but it's output \nfluctuates with load & comes with high-\nimpedance, so we feed it into U1B to \nsteady it and get rid of impedance.\n-------------------\nVBASE = 50 mV = V_out\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 115.824 135.128 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "85679b90-a364-48ad-9880-eafcf84d5e27")
	)
	(text "TRIGGER STRETCHER - U5 turns each comparator edge into a ~200 ns pulse\nU5A is a one-shot chip; A rise on makes Q go high for a `fixed time`\nC14-R16 sets this `fixed time`; larger R or C means longer\nC15 provides fast current source to Q"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 343.916 101.092 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "88bdaa9d-05cc-4d7b-9e8c-915d79a9af16")
	)
	(text "TEST POINTS - probe pads + ground loops for the scope clip"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 307.594 181.61 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a3848276-5e38-4266-b6c4-82c845c84f15")
	)
	(text "Fit R17 (stretched, default) OR R18 (direct) - never both.\nR16 + C14 set the pulse width. R7 damps the cable."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 334.01 154.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "be6f3008-c96a-4d1b-9eaf-ce947e0818b2")
	)
	(text "PEAK CAPTURE & HOLD - U3 holds the biggest pulse since the last reset, for the ADC\nU3A setup is voltage follower, but D2 ensures no backflow from C16.\nFPGA controls PEAK_RESET, which controls the Q1 switch to drain/fill C16.\nR13 (R_CHG) and C16 (C_HOLD) are bench-tuned: start at 82.0 ohm / 220 pF C0G.\nReset: fit Q1 (BSS138P, default) OR U4 (TMUX1101, precision) - never both.\nPCB: keep PEAK_HOLD tiny and ring it with a PEAK_GUARD trace."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 205.74 222.758 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "be7bd204-65ea-4208-8e4e-93b4fb1dd8d7")
	)
	(text "Pads: 2.0 mm exposed copper\n(component side).\nGround loops: two 1.0 mm holes,\n5.0 mm apart, with a bent wire.\nPut each loop within 5 mm of the\npad in the same row."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 362 192 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c21adba4-90d8-40f4-a479-513c3cb2f741")
	)
	(text "Decoupling C: Connected in parallel between the power pins \nand ground (near  an IC) to stabilize voltage and shunt high-freq noise\n--------\nThe 100n is small and fast - good at high freq. \nThe 10u holds more charge but is slower - \ngood for larger, slower load changes.\nTogether they cover a wider band than either alone.\n--------\nThe rule is: capacitor as close to the IC's supply pins \nas you can physically place it, ideally a few millimeters, \nwith a short path to ground."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 61.214 177.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ce07b5ba-3930-4c13-bedc-edf284d91ce1")
	)
	(text "C1-R2 is high pass filter\nin 1/(2πRC) ≈ 3.2 kHz range. \nMuon detection is MHz range. \nRough rule: a signal \nwith rise time τ gives 0.35/τ \nfrequency.For muon detection \nwith 100 ns pulse that's ~3.5 MHz"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.28 62.484 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e81633ca-4580-4bd3-b21c-585735245f47")
	)
	(text "U1 contains 2 independent\nhigh-gain op-amps\n------------------\nGain = 1 + R5/R6 = 13.4\n------------------\nGain-bandwidth product (GBW)\nis a number that captures an \nop-amp's speed limit, it stays\nconstant. For TPH2502, \nGBW ~ 120 MHz,\nso at 13.4 gain => usable up\nto 120/13.4 ~ 9 mHz.\n------------------\n9 MHz is within the\nrough 3x-5x headroom\nguideline for the\nsignal we want to\namplify (~3.5 mHz, see C1) \n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 193.802 104.902 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ec411f49-a3b1-4f41-93a9-aaae1345469d")
	)
	(text "C1/R2: AC coupling, \n~3.2 kHz corner"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 89.408 80.518 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f773eab6-7c1d-46b6-a1e2-aa4a1771dbb4")
	)
	(text "U2C dictates max\nand min of U2A output\n--------------\nWe want 3.3V\nbecause the FPGA\nprocessing the signals\ncan only do up to 3.3V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 258.572 164.846 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f7d5d306-db93-498f-b5ce-d81760e46726")
	)
	(text "THRESHOLD - sets the comparator trip level VTH\nRV1: potentiometer; below V_set, output is 0V, above, output is 3.3V\nC12 & C13 shunt noise to ground.\nR10/R11 limit VTH to 0-0.53 V so the 10-turn pot (3296W) gives fine steps.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 359.664 31.496 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "fae601bb-e8ae-4bb1-a8e4-2b74997c4266")
	)
